  "problemStatement": "Find the linearization of f(x) = cos(x) at a = pi/3.",
  "finalAnswer": "L(x) = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\left(x - \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)",
  "steps": [
